# requires: arch=arm64 -threaded

# pKVM Slice 3a: KVM_ENABLE_CAP(KVM_CAP_ARM_PROTECTED_VM, SET_FW_IPA) on a not-yet-run protected VM.
# syz_kvm_set_fw_ipa builds a bit-31 protected VM and issues SET_FW_IPA with a fixed page-aligned IPA,
# all in C. With a firmware region present (N90 has one) and no pkvm.handle yet, this succeeds and writes
# pvmfw_load_addr (pkvm.c:632), so the call returns 0. N90 acceptance: the call returns 0; no WARN.

r0 = openat$kvm(0xffffffffffffff9c, &AUTO='/dev/kvm\x00', 0x2, 0x0)
syz_kvm_set_fw_ipa$arm64(r0)
